@startuml quickadd_flow
' Natural-language quick-add (v21 / v21.1). See docs/design-addendum-quickadd.md
!include _style.puml
title Quick-add — three surfaces, one parse, one AI fallback (v21.2)

rectangle "surfaces" as S #EDF4F1 {
  rectangle "Activities task input\n<i>context: the selected area</i>" as IN1
  rectangle "QuickCaptureOverlay (Ctrl+N)\n<i>no context: #tag -> remembered\ndefault -> first category</i>" as IN2
}
rectangle "nlp::parseQuickAdd(text, today)\n<b>pure function</b>\ntokenize -> first-match-wins per facet:\ndate . priority . repeat . #category\nleftovers = title (casing kept)" as P
rectangle "ParsedTask\ntitle . dueDate . priority .\nrepeat . categoryHint" as PT
rectangle "quickAddPreviewHtml()\n<b>shared readout</b> — the\nsecond consumer forced the home" as PV
rectangle "commit\nAppData::categoryIdByName (domain)\n-> addTask + updateTask" as CM
database "AppData" as AD

IN1 --> P : textChanged / returnPressed
IN2 --> P : textChanged / returnPressed
P --> PT
PT ..> PV : live, every keystroke
PT --> CM : Enter
CM --> AD : one fully-dressed task
CM ..> IN2 : taskCaptured(catId)\n-> QSettings "capture memory"
rectangle "LlmQuickAddClient (wire)\nPOST /v1/messages . key read\nat request time . stale-guard" as AI
rectangle "nlp::llm (pure)\nsystemPrompt(today) .\nparseApiReply -> ParsedTask\n<i>defensive: garbage degrades</i>" as AIP
IN2 --> AI : Ctrl+Enter (explicit)
AI --> AIP : reply bytes
AIP ..> PT : same struct, \u2728 marker\nany edit disarms
note bottom of P
  same function on every path:
  no surface can disagree with
  what Enter will do
end note
@enduml
